{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>All that HaShem spoke with him on Mount Sinai.</b> All the commandments that were said during the first forty days and during the last forty days, and all the commandments that Israel were commanded were said from Nisan, in which Israel went out of Egypt, until the twentieth of Iyyar in the second year. But the Torah scroll reveals — since Moses would hear the commandments from the mouth of HaShem, he would write each one in its own separate scroll, and when he came to depart from the world, he arranged a Torah scroll and fixed in it the parashiyyot until this day, according to the adjacent portions fitting for them, as our rabbis expounded."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:56.179639466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}